uu(a){return"Note: "+a+" has the two groups the wrong way round \u2014 the AI samples scored lower, not higher \u2014 so its weight drops to zero. That usually means the engine does not suit this kind of text."},
guq(){return"Apply the learned weights"},
guo(){return"Learned weights applied"},
gur(){return"Weights come from how well each engine separates your human samples from your AI ones (Cohen's d effect size): the further apart the two groups, and the steadier each group is, the more weight that engine earns. This replaces the hand-set fixed weights so the ensemble fits the kind of text you actually work with."},
